{
  "name": "Jump",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/skills/movement/figure-running-gray.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you make a Long Jump, you leap horizontally a number of feet up to your Strength score if you move at least 10 feet immediately before the jump. When you make a standing Long Jump, you can leap only half that distance. Either way, each foot you jump costs a foot of movement.</p><p>If you land in Difficult Terrain, you must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check or have the Prone condition.</p><p><em>Macro Helper</em> : the squares you can land on show green, the ones you pass over yellow. Click a green one : a standing jump, a running jump, or a running jump with its run-up walked first, whichever gets you there. Part of your move, no action.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
